  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find the GCF, we list the factors of the coefficients and identify any common variable factors in the expressions.\n\nThe factors of $4$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,4.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $2$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2.\n$$\n\nThe common factors of $4$ and $2$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2.\n$$\n\nThe greatest of these common factors is $2.$\n\nNow we look at the variable factors. Both $4x$ and $2x$ contain $x.$\n\nThus, the greatest common factor of $4x$ and $2x$ is $2x.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
